<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:17:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Deceived and deployed: How young Cameroonians end up fighting in Russia's war in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54eb7dc5a2c5057f4a2c6755fd0e080956a5c822c31d0388fc2e8b403a134424</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:17:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deceived-and-deployed-how-young-cameroonians-end-up-fighting-in-russia-s-war-in-ukraine/a-78513256--36e5a7bb7687.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deceived-and-deployed-how-young-cameroonians-end-up-fighting-in-russia-s-war-in-ukraine/a-78513256?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts say economic desperation and fraudulent recruitment schemes are funneling Cameroonian youth into the Russian military — with deadly consequences. Does the Cameroonian government need to act more decisively?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Niger's failed coup exposes cracks in the military — and Russia's influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eede96cffb95650471fa4c4b376756a1db88e099295924e177b54034dc24b2d9</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:17:45Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T11:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/niger-s-failed-coup-exposes-cracks-in-the-military-and-russia-s-influence/a-78572278--9b38e93b8134.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/niger-s-failed-coup-exposes-cracks-in-the-military-and-russia-s-influence/a-78572278?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The failed coup in Niger has brought deep divisions within the military to light. As Russia's support highlights the junta's fading influence, soldiers continue to face jihadi attacks, poor equipment and little pay.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Passengers stranded amid airport staff strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea8c85de97663cd9b2494e76811a46ebe297ccae548e7bcf41ba000174b58782</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:17:48Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-passengers-stranded-amid-airport-staff-strike/a-78570644--3ae5fd5fdeec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-passengers-stranded-amid-airport-staff-strike/a-78570644?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Airport workers are staging a work slow-down to protest poor working conditions and a lack of support from relevant authorities.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkish, Somali forces free vessel seized by pirates in Somalia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61b4f11023802ef7ceeac55c5883cee844da07fc0cb924038e37ad88162983dc</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:20Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T20:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkish-somali-forces-free-vessel-seized-by-pirates-in-somalia/a-78560087--de7714620edd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkish-somali-forces-free-vessel-seized-by-pirates-in-somalia/a-78560087?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish and Somali forces have freed the MV LUTUF after pirates hijacked the vessel off the coast of Somalia. The 10-day operation killed 14 alleged pirates and destroyed four boats used by the attackers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Zimbabwe crash involving church minibus kills 27</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a9b545a5ff9762d6be1b1973d4efc0fc7b9c77ec6a3ba4390482fcc2ce22b97</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:20Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T17:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-crash-involving-church-minibus-kills-27/a-78558710--108e8ca003fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-crash-involving-church-minibus-kills-27/a-78558710?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of people were killed when a minibus carrying churchgoers collided head-on with a truck in central Zimbabwe. The crash near the town of Chivhu is the latest deadly road accident in the African country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's aging autocrats fight to stay in power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c02fe06a7e0a5c5bd31a8c1a157766ed31ace95496181efffe295a36ca4979d</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:20Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-aging-autocrats-fight-to-stay-in-power/a-78487210--45be184aa17e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-aging-autocrats-fight-to-stay-in-power/a-78487210?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As some of Africa's longest-serving leaders grow older, they are using different tactics to extend their rule. But age, succession battles and public pressure pose new challenges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What does Saxony-Anhalt's election mean for migrants?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b10edc53fbf792b79a0e5e72e3f37f203a5f5826eba95706072f308b80173fe</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:20Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-does-saxony-anhalt-s-election-mean-for-migrants/a-78504553--ae71d2d9cd41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-does-saxony-anhalt-s-election-mean-for-migrants/a-78504553?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD could make history in the German state of Saxony-Anhalt. For many people with a migration background, the September 6 state election raises questions about belonging, security and their future in Germany.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f6538eb7b83854331338a9752adad5869883d6921e2dc07dc39f80c517ef46b</id><updated>2026-08-31T16:14:20Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--a9305ea94714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry></feed>
